Draw the **sonar pulse**, an 8-frame **sprite sheet** of an expanding ring
effect, using only the drawing tool.

The sonar pulse is the **expanding ring** a deep-sea forager and the eyeless
Listener predator both emit in a maze-chase game — an area effect that spreads
across many tiles, far larger than a creature sprite, which is why it has a large
canvas of its own. Draw it as one ring growing outward from the center and
fading, frame by frame. Draw it **purely in grayscale on transparency**: the game
tints it to the sonar color at runtime, so you supply only the shape and
brightness of the wavefront, never any hue.

## How drawing works

The only way to make a mark is the `draw-sheet` binary already on your `PATH`.
You build the sheet by calling it **one operation at a time**, each targeting a
frame with `--frame <index>`. The ordered operations you issue are recorded to a
per-frame action log, and that log is your submission.

Each frame is its **own separate 128×128 image**. After each call the binary
re-renders that frame to `frames/<index>.png` and appends the operation to that
frame's log. Blank starting frames and empty logs are already in place at
`{{workspace}}`.

Each operation is an ordinary subcommand with flags, naming its frame:

```
draw-sheet stroke-circle --frame 0 --cx 64 --cy 64 --r 10 --color "#ffffff"
```

Run `draw-sheet --help` to list every operation and `draw-sheet <operation>
--help` for one operation's exact flags — that help text is the authoritative
contract. **Read `frames/<index>.png` after your calls** to see your progress and
decide what to do next.

## What to read first

The full specification is in the `specs/` directory at `{{workspace}}`, already
present in your project. Read all of it before you start, and produce an
implementation that matches the specification exactly.

## What to deliver

Build the pulse up operation by operation until each `frames/<index>.png` matches
the brief: a clean ring centered on (64, 64), small and bright in frame 0,
expanding outward and fading to a wide faint ring by frame 7, drawn only in
grayscale on full transparency. Played in order the frames must read as one
sonar wavefront traveling out. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded
per-frame action logs are your finished submission.
